From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlmarionAI <150292831+AlmarionAI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:04:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [principal] sealed agent principal and fail-closed
 principal gate

Add GUC_SEALED, a core GUC flag enforced in set_config_with_handle(): a
sealed variable holding a value refuses every assignment and reset, and
may only be established by the connected session itself (never by a
role/database default, the command line, the environment or the startup
packet).

Add agent_principal, a sealed GUC carrying "agent=<id>,org=<id>" in one
value, so agent and org are established by a single assignment and sealed
as a group: a frontend can never leave a half-set principal for the agent
to complete. current_agent() and current_org() expose the two fields.

When agent_principal_secret (superuser-only, never accepted from a catalog
or the startup packet) is set, the principal must also carry
",sig=<hex HMAC-SHA256(secret, "agent=<id>,org=<id>")>", so a session that
does not know the secret cannot establish any principal at all.

Add agent_require_principal (PGC_SUSET), which makes standard_ExecutorStart
refuse any plan while no principal is sealed. Bump MAX_GUC_FLAGS 6 -> 7 to
match the push sites in pg_settings_get_flags. Regression test
agent_identity.
